# Demo Detail Page Section Order

Every demo detail page MUST render sections in this exact order:

1. **Description** — lead paragraph (first text in the markdown body)
2. **Workflow** — Mermaid diagram (if present, moved via JS into the body)
3. **Video walkthrough** — YouTube embed (if present, moved via JS into the body)
4. **Prerequisites** — `## Prerequisites` in the markdown
5. **Configure credentials before first run** — `## Configure credentials` (if present)
6. **Survey prompts** — `## Survey prompts` table
7. **Job templates** — `## Job templates` table
8. **Why it matters** — `## Why it matters` (if present)
9. **Presenter walkthrough** — `## Presenter walkthrough` (if present)
10. **Talking points** — `## Talking points` (if present)
11. **See other \<category\> demos** — layout CTA linking to `/?category=<category>` (Pages strips markdown `## Related demos` tables)

Description ALWAYS comes first. Workflow and Video come between the description and Prerequisites. Never reorder these sections.

The layout renders Workflow and Video as separate `<section>` elements after `{{ content }}`. JavaScript in `demo-toc.js` moves them into `.detail-body` between the lead paragraph and the first `<h2>` heading.

Source READMEs may still include `## Related demos` for GitHub browsing; the Pages build removes them and injects the category CTA instead.

When writing new demo markdown files in `<section>/docs/`, follow this heading order.
